18-
19:Colour relationship: white stucco / dark timber / pale grey roof frame; tan stone, orange door (and orange upholstery inside) and teal car as accents. Interiors: warm spruce + white + orange and teal touches.
20-
21-## VOCABULARY (helpers; each takes world coordinates; "set" = only into air, per runParts)
22-
--
46-- `garden_lamp(x,z)`: dark_oak_fence y=1..2, lantern (hanging=false) y=3 (x,z on sand/lawn, base y=1).
47:- `hung_lantern(x,y=4,z)` below a beam: lantern hanging=true (see Interior).
48-
49:**Interior**
50-- `terrazzo_floor(box)`: smooth_stone with seeded flecks.
51-- `panel_wall(x,y0..y1,z,facing)`: open spruce_trapdoors on the wall, half alternating bottom/top; ~3 high strips.
52-- `hung_lantern(x,z)`: lantern hanging=true at y=4 (needs a block at y=5: a beam line cell or the ceiling).
--
59-- `dining_set(x,z)`: table = spruce_slab top at y=2 on 4 spruce_fence legs (2x3); six chairs = birch_stairs facing the table; pendant = lantern hanging from the beam above.
60:- `galley_kitchen`: counters = smooth_quartz_slab/white_concrete row at y=2 with smoker/furnace/cauldron as appliances; upper cabinets spruce_trapdoor; breakfast bar = spruce_slab top at y=2 on spruce_fence legs; bar stools = birch_slab on iron_trapdoor posts? use dark_oak_fence + birch_slab bottom.
61-- `bed_double(x,z,facing,color)`: a bed block pair (orange_bed etc.), headboard of spruce_planks 1 high behind it, nightstands birch_slab on spruce_fence.
62-- `wardrobe(x,z,len,axis)`: spruce_planks 2 high + open spruce_trapdoor fronts.
63-- `bath_fit`: tub = cauldron? No: tub = 2 smooth_quartz_slab bottom + water? Use quartz stairs and slab shell with `water` inside (1 deep), basin = cauldron on a quartz pillar? simple: basin = cauldron, mirror = glass_pane, WC = quartz_stairs.
--
66-
67:Interior shell: floor y=1 (finished, standing y=2), perimeter walls x=10, x=31, z=8, z=25, interior partitions white_concrete y=2..4 only, ceiling spruce_planks y=5 at z=9..13 and z=20..24 (not on beam lines, not over the atrium or chimney); over z=14..19 the room is open up to the roof (y up to 6). Room boxes below list air y=2..4 (y=1..4 where the floor is sunk).
68-
69-| room | box [x0,y0,z0,x1,y1,z1] | floor | ways in |
70-|---|---|---|---|
71:| gallery | [16,2,10,22,4,10] | terrazzo | front door (19,2..3,9); atrium doors (19..20,2..3,11); kitchen at x=16 z=9..10 open; corridor at x=22 z=9..10 open |
72:| kitchen | [11,2,9,15,4,13] | terrazzo | open at x=16 z=9..10 to the gallery; utility door (10,2..3,10) from the carport; open on its south side to dining along z=13/14 (breakfast bar line) |
73:| dining | [11,2,14,15,4,18] | terrazzo | open to kitchen (z=13/14) and to living (z=18/19); window x=10 z=14..16 y=3..4 |
74-| living (with pit and fireplace) | [11,2,19,21,4,24] (pit x=13..17 z=20..23 is y=1..4 with floor y=0) | terrazzo, pit smooth_quartz | open to dining on z=18/19; atrium doors (19..20,2..3,18); doorway (22,2..4,19..20) east to the corridor; sliders (14..15,2..3,25), (20..21,2..3,25) |
75-| atrium | [17,1,12,21,4,17] | dirt and grass (open sky) | atrium doors (19..20,2..3,11) from the gallery and (19..20,2..3,18) from the living room |
76-| corridor | [23,2,9,24,4,21] | terrazzo | gallery at x=22 z=9..10; living doorway (22,19..20); master bedroom open at z=21/22; doorways (25,2..3,10) bed1, (25,2..3,15) bath 1, (25,2..3,19) bed 2 |
--
86-- gallery: narrow entrance hall, wood-lined (panel_wall on the south side is the ring glass: use the north wall), a low bench (birch_slab on spruce_fence) and a lantern; sees the atrium through the glass doors.
87:- kitchen: galley along the north wall z=9..10 (counter, hob, fridge as iron_block + trapdoors), breakfast bar on the south side with stools, orange accent; utility door west.
88-- dining: round-feeling table for six, sideboard on the west wall under the window, pendant lantern.
89-- living: the show room: sofa_low x2 (orange) around the pit, egg chair by the atrium glass, tulip side table, freestanding fireplace as the focus, sideboard, floor lamp (end_rod on fence), wood panelling on the x=22 partition.
90-- atrium: green court: grass patch, large ferns, potted cactus, a small jungle sapling tree, 3-wide stepping path, bench; keep the doors' cells x=19..20 free.
--
98-
99:1. **parts/shell.mjs, house shell and ground**: dirt at y=-1 over x=0..33 z=0..33 except pool cells (RESERVED); dirt y=0 under the house footprint and atrium; floor y=1 over x=10..31 z=8..25 (terrazzo in public rooms, spruce_planks bedrooms, smooth_quartz baths, none on the pit x=13..17 z=20..23 and the atrium and the chimney; smooth_quartz at y=0 in the pit); perimeter walls: base smooth_stone y=1, body white_concrete y=2..4, header dark_oak_planks y=5 SKIPPING beam-line cells (see header_course); leave every OPENINGS cell as air (entry niche, clerestory cells, windows, sliders, door gaps, ring); door wall z=9 x=17..21 as described; atrium ring walls as dark_oak_planks header + air body for part 4; interior partitions and doorways per ROOMS; ceiling spruce_planks y=5 per ROOMS. Ticks 1, 7, 13 (gaps), 16 (shell).
100-2. **parts/site.mjs, ground cover and carport**: sidewalk, driveway with joint rows, sand yard, gravel beds, stepping pads, landing, sand strips, carport (`carport`, `breeze_screen`), patio, pool deck, lawns (patio and deck first, lawn only into air; pool cells untouched), x=9 z=8..25 sand. Ticks 5, 6, 11, 18, 19, 24 (paving), 25.
101-3. **parts/roofs.mjs, roof, beams, chimney**: the 4 bands with `roof_band` and `fascia_ring`, `beam_line` x 10, 13, ..., 31 plus x=10 and x=31 wall lines, gable-end glass at y=6 (x=10 and x=31, z=14..19) and ring glass at y=6 (x=16 and x=22, z=14..17), the dark_oak_slab hole edge. Fireplace stack at x=20..21 z=21..22: y=1 mud_bricks; y=2 (20,2,21) and (20,2,22) campfire lit=true, (21,2,21) and (21,2,22) mud_bricks; y=3 mud_bricks 2x2 lintel; y=4..7 black_concrete 2x2 flue; y=8 smooth_stone_slab bottom cap. Ticks 2, 3, 14.
102-4. **parts/facades.mjs, glazing, posts, entry, feature wall**: `glass_bay` for the south wall, ring, windows; `post` on every beam line of the south wall, 4 corners, ring corners and x=19 at y=4 (lintel); `slider_gap` glazing at y=4; `clerestory`; `orange_entry` with the acacia_door; `ledgestone_wall` and its cap; utility door (dark_oak_door open) at (10,2,10). Ticks 4, 7, 8, 9, 10, 12, 13, 15, 16.
--
113-- The atrium door cells (x=19..20, y=2..3, z=11 and z=18) win over the x=19 post: part 4 puts the post at y=4 only there.
114:- Room boxes are the air the interior designers may fill; keep doorway cells, the pit, and one-block paths clear. Do not put furniture on door cells.
115-- The architect's RESERVED cells are for the named parts only. The car and palms are in the front yard; palm (30,4)'s crown meets the roof at z=6: skip cells that are already filled.
116-- No colored full block stands in for an object. Use stairs, slabs, trapdoors, carpet.
117-- Part 1 (shell) notes: build.mjs lays dirt at y=0 over the whole lot before the parts, so the shell does not rewrite the dirt under the house or atrium; the pit's y=0 cells are overwritten to smooth_quartz. The shell leaves air, for later parts to fill: the whole south wall body y=2..4 (x=10..31, z=25: glass, posts, sliders), the corner cells (10/31, z=8 and z=25) for part 4's posts, the clerestory row y=4 x=22..30 at z=8, the atrium ring body, and the entry niche plus door cells (x=18..20, z=9). The door wall z=9 x=17 and x=21 are stucco.
----
